    { title: `MA and energy`, content: `$$MA=W/E=800/500=1.6=\\frac{\\text{effort arm}}{\\text{load arm}}=2/1.25=1.6$$ Girl lifting boy: girl's $$PE$$ loss $$mgh$$ converts to boy's $$KE$$ then $$PE$$ gain, ideal $$W_{in}=W_{out}$$ energy conserved, real friction heat loss.` }
